## 1. Site (iii): three plan statements still say "the binder's PRC". They should be struck.

The plan carries **two incompatible specifications of row 7 in the same document**, and one of them
is inside the same bullet as the other:

| where | says | status |
|---|---|---|
| **L482** | "drop the Score factor and tie-break on the **binding** analyzer's PRC (`combineVotes` binder, `up=false`), then name ascending" | **stale** |
| **L484-487** (same bullet, added by the 2026-08-07 refresh) | "Row 7's unit is *dimensionless coverage per GPU freed*, and the operator is `max_i`, never `Σ_i`" | **authority** |
| **L1721-1722** (§5 dev-guide bullet) | "**C6c** (iii) (`sortVariantsForScaleDown` tie-break: Score dropped, uses the binder's PRC)" | **stale, twice** — wrong mechanism *and* wrong commit label (site (iii) moved to C6d per L479 and the §0 row at L283) |
| **L1013** (§2d.6 `[sat]`-only table, row (iii)) | "exactly identical … the replacement reads the `combineVotes(up=false)` binder's PRC, which with one vote **is** `PRC_sat[v]`" | **stale mechanism**, and the conclusion is now **conditionally** false — see below |

**These are not two wordings of one rule; they select different analyzers.** For `up=false`
`combineVotes`' binder is the entry with the **minimum** `spare/prc` — it coincides with the
maximum-PRC entry only when every voter's spare happens to be equal. And the Type 1's row 7 adds a
**`GPUsPerReplica` division** that the "binder's PRC" formulation never mentions at all.

I resolved this by the plan's own tie-break rule (§2d.5 L943-954: *"the Type 1's `W5` is the
authority; if this table and it ever disagree, the Type 1 governs"*) and implemented
**`maxᵢ PRC_i[v] ÷ GPUsPerReplica[v]`, ascending**, Score absent, name-ascending as the final tie.
Requesting that L482, L1721 and L1013's justification be **struck** rather than left standing as
apparent authority — same treatment §2 #5 site (v) got in C6c.

### 1b. L1013's "exactly identical" is now a qualified claim, not an unconditional one

Row 7 with one analyzer:

- old key: `Σ_i voteScore_i × PRC_i[v]` = `1.0 × PRC_sat[v]`
- new key: `maxᵢ PRC_i[v] / GPUsPerReplica[v]` = `PRC_sat[v] / GPUsPerReplica[v]`

Ascending order over these two keys **differs whenever a role's cost-tied variants do not share
`GPUsPerReplica`** — which is exactly the case the division was introduced to fix. So the cell
should read *"identical **only when the role's cost-tied variants share `GPUsPerReplica`**; a
`[sat]`-only model with same-cost, differently-sized variants reorders — deliberately"*, not
"exactly identical".

This does **not** weaken the goldens signal: the tie-break only fires on an exact `Cost` tie, no
#1513 golden has one, and none moved. But the table is read as the definition of what a moving
golden would mean, so it should be true.

