## 2. `applyDeallocationForRole` materialized map keys — a defect the plan does not name, and
## C6d's veto turns it from inert into a wrong-answer bug

Pre-C6d the function did a bare `s[i].RoleSpare[role] -= float64(n) * prc`. On a map with **no such
key** that reads the zero value, subtracts, clamps to 0, and **writes** — i.e. it *creates* the key
at `0`.

Under N7 (`C7`) a **missing** key is an **abstain** and a **present `<= 0`** is a **veto**. So after
the first removal in a role, an analyzer that never sized that role would hold an explicit `0` and
C6d's PRC-blind, score-blind veto would block **every remaining variant in the loop** — the plan's
own stated invariant ("key missing ⇒ abstain") would be false from the second iteration onward.

Fixed with a key-presence guard:

```go
spare, ok := s[i].RoleSpare[role]
if !ok {
    continue // abstained on this role (N7): no reported balance to spend
}
```

**Observationally inert before C6d** (`votesFromRoleSpare` reads an absent key and a present `0`
identically), which is why the pre-existing form was harmless and is not any longer — and why it
moves no golden. Recorded in the doc comment and in the dev guide's *"An absent key is a different
statement from a present zero"* paragraph. Flagging it as an **implementation-required addition the
plan did not name**, so §2d.4 (c) can pick it up as part of the finding rather than as an
undocumented extra.

---

## 3. The collector-level N7 hole is still open, and its in-code deferral note now predates the
## two commits that make it matter

`votesFromRoleSpare` does **not** check key presence, so an analyzer that abstained on a role still
**casts a `0` vote** in the ballot. Under the **uniform scores that actually ship**, `e = 0` binds
and `combineVotes` returns `0` — removal is throttled to zero. That is an *effective* veto from an
abstention, which is precisely what N7 says must not happen.

C7 honored N7 at the **role-entry gate**; C6d honors it at the **per-variant veto**. Neither touches
the ballot. The in-code comment defers this as *"a behavioral question, not part of hoisting the
arithmetic into one place"* — but that note **predates both C6b (scores can now outvote a `0`) and
C7 (which gave abstain-vs-veto a name)**, so it is deferring against a premise that has changed
twice.

**I did not change behavior** — out of C6d's scope and it is the kind of edit that should not ride
along silently. What I did do: corrected `votesFromRoleSpare`' doc comment (the old text claimed a
map-miss vote *"holds removal at zero"*, which post-C6b is false in general) and corrected the dev
guide's collectors table, which falsely claimed all three collectors require "its own state for that
role" — in fact `votesFromTotalDemand` drops an entry that doesn't decompose the role while the other
two read the map-miss as `0`.

**Safe today**: a spurious `0` can only **under**-remove. So this is a re-decision request, not a
blocker. Candidate homes: fold into C6f (`W4` is the same shape — "no basis ⇒ no participation"), or
its own commit.

